; exit 31 (see .exit)
; MM-LIFE-2g, the CURRIED half: a lambda's outer parameter is a
; CAPTURE by the time a store inside the body runs, and the word that
; classifies it belongs to an application one level out.
;
; WHY THIS IS A SEPARATE FILE FROM 460. Not taste - arithmetic.
; `460-closure-reclaim.ax` reports through its exit status, one bit per
; term, and a process exit code is EIGHT BITS. 460 uses all of them
; (1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128 = 255), so a ninth term there is not a
; ninth bit: it is `511 & 0xFF`, which is 255, and the fixture would
; have gone on reporting success while asserting one more thing than it
; could say. Measured that way first, before this file existed.
;
; WHAT IT PINS. `(lambda (a b) ..)` is `(lambda (a) (lambda (b) ..))`
; by the parser, so a body storing `a` runs inside the INNER lambda and
; reads `a` out of the closure record. `MM-LIFE-2g`'s share is stamped
; from an evidence word, and each lifted lambda has one for its OWN
; argument - so the inner lambda's word is about `b`, and `a`'s is the
; word the outer application passed. Until those words were made to
; travel by depth, a store of `a` took no share:
;
;   2  the OUTER parameter of a two-parameter lambda, parked and then
;      read back after the struct field it came from is overwritten.
;      Event 5 releases the only counted share; an uncounted park then
;      reads a string allocated after the free. It read 122 - `z` -
;      where 97 is the `a` that was recorded.
;   4  the INNER parameter of the same shape, which was always correct
;      and must stay so: it is the lambda's own argument, at depth 0.
;   8  the OUTERMOST parameter of a THREE-parameter lambda, two levels
;      out, because the rule is a depth and not a special case for one.
;  16  and the MIDDLE one of those three, at depth 1.
;   1  every step above ran.
;
; The two-and-three split is the discrimination: a fix that carried one
; level would pass 2 and 4 and fail 8.
;
; MEASURED AGAINST THE COMPILER THAT PREDATES THE FIX, three runs each:
; this file exits 31 built by the tree and **139** built by the
; compiler one commit back - a SEGMENTATION FAULT, not a wrong byte.
; Each shape on its own reads 122, the first byte of a string
; allocated into the freed block; four of them in one process recycle
; blocks into each other until a header read lands outside the heap.
; That difference is worth stating because it is the honest shape of
; this defect: an uncounted park is not a value that reads oddly, it
; is a pointer whose block has been handed to someone else, and what
; happens next depends on who got it.
(import Str)

(import Vec)

(struct Holder
  (name : String))

(:: b2i (-> Bool Int))

(fn (b2i x)
  (if x
    1
    0
  )
)

; One probe, parameterised by which of a curried lambda's arguments is
; the one that came out of the struct field. `pick` names it so the
; reader can see the four cases differ in exactly that.
(:: parkedByte (-> Int Int))

(fn (parkedByte pick)
  (let ((log vecNew))
    (let ((h (Holder (strDup "alice"))))
      {
        (if (== pick 0)
          ((lambda (a b) (vecPush log a)) h.name 0)
          (if (== pick 1)
            ((lambda (a b) (vecPush log b)) 0 h.name)
            (if (== pick 2)
              ((lambda (a b c) (vecPush log a)) h.name 0 1)
              ((lambda (a b c) (vecPush log b)) 0 h.name 1)
            )
          )
        )
        ; Event 5: the field's only counted share goes.
        (set h.name (strDup "bob"))
        ; Allocated after it, so a freed block is handed back here and
        ; the read below sees these bytes instead.
        (strDup "zzzzz")
        (strByte (vecGetStr log 0) 0)
      }
    )
  )
)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main)
  (let ((mut acc 0) (mut steps 0))
    {
      ; 2 - the outer parameter of two
      (set acc (+ acc (* 2 (b2i (== (parkedByte 0) 97)))))
      (set steps (+ steps 1))
      ; 4 - the inner parameter of two, at depth 0
      (set acc (+ acc (* 4 (b2i (== (parkedByte 1) 97)))))
      (set steps (+ steps 1))
      ; 8 - the outermost of three, at depth 2
      (set acc (+ acc (* 8 (b2i (== (parkedByte 2) 97)))))
      (set steps (+ steps 1))
      ; 16 - the middle of three, at depth 1
      (set acc (+ acc (* 16 (b2i (== (parkedByte 3) 97)))))
      (set steps (+ steps 1))
      (if (== steps 4)
        (+ acc 1)
        acc
      )
    }
  )
)
